  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 > pca_n2000, multiprofile > singleprofile, transformer ≥ avgpool, weighted > concat, and imagenet_vit_l > resnet50. However, the scgpt RNA encoder has never been tested in any multimodal or multiprofile setting. Config_051 isolates the effect of RNA encoder (scgpt vs scvi_n200) while holding all other components at their empirically best settings. This is the highest-value remaining question: if scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new direction for the final experiment; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as optimal and solidifies our confidence in config_039 as the final answer. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, testing the single unexplored encoder in the proven-best architecture is the most informative use of the slot."
